!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/an-enum-member-that-is-not-a-name-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §7.4, [TSON-DATA] §7.7"
  description: """
    `enum.profile` defaults to IDENTIFIER, under which every member must match [TSON-DATA] §7.7's
    grammar. `lightly active` holds a space, so it is not a name and the body contradicts its own
    declaration -- a schema-load error, in the family of coherence errors §7.2 makes a compilation
    concern rather than data validation.

    The companion valid vector writes the same member set with `profile: TEXT` and resolves. What this
    one guards is that the default is the strict reading: a processor defaulting to TEXT would accept
    this document and would, in doing so, have dropped §8.2's restricted-character and
    restricted-script rules from every enum in existence without anything being written down.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
